# The C99 tree's formatting contract (AUD-0010).
#
# Before this file the C tree's style was hand-maintained and never machine-checked, so a
# contributor had no way to know what "formatted" meant and no gate could say whether they
# had achieved it. `C99/scripts/check-format.sh` runs this config over the tracked C sources
# and fails on any difference.
#
# The settings are chosen to describe the style the tree already has rather than to replace
# it, so the reformat this file accompanies is a normalisation and not a restyle:
#
#   IndentWidth 2            the tree is written with two-space indents
#   ColumnLimit 100          the tree's hand wrapping sits just under 100, and 100 changes
#                            fewer files than 120 while leaving every line at or below the
#                            width the maintainers already chose
#   IndentCaseLabels true    `case` labels are indented inside their `switch`, as in the tree
#   AllowShortCaseLabelsOnASingleLine false
#                            a case body stays on its own line; collapsing it would rewrite
#                            every small accessor in the tree for no readability gain
#   AllowShortIfStatementsOnASingleLine AllIfsAndElse
#                            `if (out == NULL) return WT_ERR_INVALID_ARGUMENT;` is the tree's
#                            established guard idiom and stays on one line
#   AllowShortFunctionsOnASingleLine None
#                            functions stay multi-line even when short, matching the tree
#   ReflowComments false     comments are hand-wrapped to fit their subject; a reflow would
#                            rewrite prose that is deliberately shaped
---
Language: Cpp
BasedOnStyle: LLVM
IndentWidth: 2
ColumnLimit: 100
IndentCaseLabels: true
AllowShortCaseLabelsOnASingleLine: false
AllowShortIfStatementsOnASingleLine: AllIfsAndElse
AllowShortFunctionsOnASingleLine: None
ReflowComments: false
